# Paths are matched from the build-context root, so every pattern that should also catch nested folders carries
# `**/`: a bare `data`, `dist`, `.claude` or `test-results` matches only at the root, and a development tree's
# apps/api/data/v2/session.secret must never reach the image.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/data
.git
# Every .env sibling: the runtime never reads these
# files (Compose passes .env through env_file), and a backup copy such as
# .env.bak would carry secrets into the image layers. .env.example is excluded
# too; it is documentation, not an input.
**/.env*
*.md
# Documentation: no code under apps/ or packages/ reads docs/ at
# runtime or at build, so none of it belongs in the image.
docs
# Host-side deployment files never belong in the image; TLS material is mounted at run time.
deploy
certs
# Never runtime inputs: local tool settings and Playwright output.
**/.claude
**/test-results
